- `ConfirmedPickerModal` has a full-screen backdrop `Pressable` with `${testID}-backdrop` that calls `onDone`. Post-integration gates passed: `pnpm verify` 40 suites/270 tests, coverage (87.08% statements), and React Doctor 100/100; `.maestro/flows/reminder-owned-timing.yaml` parsed successfully. [Task 2]
- Expo map refresh reported 18 routes, 2 layouts, 30 screenshots, and 22 flows. `.expo-map/Youmotion-2026-08-20.appmap` is authoritative: `render-map.mjs` fails on format-v2 object flow steps with `TypeError: (f.steps ?? []).map is not a function`. Rebase, fast-forward, and push were verified at `afc5ce53874595dfd3055e77a7e5501f1f998c96`. [Task 2]
- The emotion check-in addition must reuse the local-first, assignment-owned subsystem: native requests remain derived projections, Pulse routes to `/today`, and notification taps route through the root navigation actor. Relevant paths are `src/features/reminders/`, `src/features/settings/ui/settings-screen.tsx`, `.maestro/flows/`, `docs/reminders-runtime-test-matrix.md`, and `docs/handoffs/`. [Task 4]
- The feature added localized Settings/reminder UI, focused tests, redacted Maestro lifecycle `.maestro/flows/emotion-check-in-reminder.yaml`, English/German screenshots, runtime/README/AGENTS updates, and `docs/handoffs/emotion-check-in-reminder.md` while preserving current reminder behavior. `pnpm verify` passed 40 suites/273 tests, Oxlint, and TypeScript 7. [Task 4]
- The current map artifact is `.expo-map/Youmotion-2026-08-21.appmap`: valid ZIP, unchanged graph (18 routes, 2 layouts, 0 edges), 22 flows, and 31 screenshots. Main and `origin/codex/emotion-check-in-reminder` were read back at `399fbbe4ec3767442620eeecaa8ba2784eac13f8` after a no-op rebase and `git merge --ff-only`. [Task 4]
- `src/features/reminders/ui/leitsatz-reminder-screen.tsx` reserves the `reminder-schedule-name-guidance-slot` at `minHeight: 38`; its regression test is `src/features/reminders/__tests__/leitsatz-reminder-screen.test.tsx`. Live iOS QA confirmed `TAGE` and `ZEIT` stay fixed while typing; `pnpm verify` passed 242 tests, coverage passed, and React Doctor scored 91/100 with one mapped-list warning in `reminder-settings-screen.tsx:55`. [Task 3]
- Commit only owned paths when unrelated artifacts exist. Commit `75496fdeb6fde1e081d9fa3978d142e312e970ee` was pushed to `codex/leitsatz-reminders`; EAS group `bad01098-0aad-46c1-9720-7384647e1835` was read back for Android/iOS at runtime `1.0.2` and the exact commit. Publish from a clean clone pinned to the pushed SHA with `CI=true pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --package-import-method=hardlink`; then use the existing `skills/youmotion-eas-update/SKILL.md` procedure. [Task 3]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: a hosted visual plan is required but cannot publish. Cause: the Plan connector is unavailable. Fix: do not improvise inline output; reconnect with `npx -y @agent-native/core@latest reconnect https://plan.agent-native.com --client codex`, restart, and publish through Plan. [Task 1]
- Symptom: persisted intent appears active while native reminders are wrong. Cause: requests were treated as stored truth. Fix: fingerprint/diff derived requests and run lifecycle/physical-device coverage for permission denial/revocation, foreground/background/terminated, reboot, update, timezone/DST, locale, test deep links, Android force-stop, stale targets, and Watch claims only after physical validation. [Task 1]
- Symptom: schedules are technically copied per reminder but UI/domain still exposes reusable names. Fix: remove the conceptual and persistence-level schedule abstraction, not only copy schedules. [Task 2]
- Symptom: Maestro reports `Unable to launch app com.youmotion.mobile: UNAVAILABLE: io exception` or Harness reports no Metro port in `8084-8093`. Cause: pre-flow environment failure. Fix: do not claim native validation; retry on a healthy dedicated target. The Expo map request was completed and included in the verified `.appmap` bundle. [Task 2]
