### keywords

- emotion check-in reminder, Pulse, emotion-check-in-reminder.yaml, reminders-runtime-test-matrix.md, docs/handoffs/emotion-check-in-reminder.md, emotion-check-in-*.png, 399fbbe, pnpm verify, Oxlint, TypeScript 7, .expo-map/Youmotion-2026-08-21.appmap

## User preferences

- when discussing reminders, the user required “a broken reminder is worse than no reminder” plus test reminders, DST/timezone handling, reboot/update/permission/locale testing, and direct Pulse navigation -> make reliability, recovery, deep-link QA, and non-guilt copy explicit acceptance criteria [Task 1]
- when asking “can I do it completely local/local-first?” -> prefer device-local privacy-first architecture before adding backend synchronization [Task 1]
- when the user asked to “activate daily notifications” and “set a schedule” -> make selectable days/times core scope rather than later polish [Task 1]
- when the user said reminders should not “pop up at the same time” -> default to independent per-reminder days/times, not reusable named schedules [Task 2]
- when the user wanted general-vs-Leitsatz content immediately after the emotion flow -> make privacy/content choice part of reminder creation, not only settings [Task 2]
- when the user asked to “make every notable step cherry pickable,” add screenshots for UI-changing commits, and update documentation/handoffs -> preserve isolated commits, visual evidence, and executable docs [Task 2]
- when the user required clicking outside modals to close them -> use backdrop dismissal for modal/picker UI [Task 2]
- when implementing a new feature, the user required “for each feature you create there must be a e2e test,” mocked/redacted production data, documentation, and a handoff MD document -> plan saved E2E coverage, privacy-safe fixtures, executable docs, and handoff alongside implementation rather than as follow-up polish [Task 4]

## Reusable knowledge

- Youmotion uses Expo SDK 57, Expo Router/XState navigation, and local SurrealDB. Settings persist through `src/features/settings/infrastructure/app-settings.repository.ts`; Pulse is `/today`, centrally projected by `src/navigation/app-navigation.machine.ts` and `src/navigation/app-router.adapter.ts`. [Task 1]
- Persist wall-clock `{hour, minute}` and selected weekdays. Native notification requests are derived projections: reconcile only Youmotion-owned requests using stable assignment/schedule/target/day/time/locale/content fingerprints; never call `cancelAllScheduledNotificationsAsync()`. A backend is unnecessary for on-device schedules; add one only for cross-device sync, remote push/server-managed schedules, account recovery, or analytics. [Task 1]
- Route notification taps through the root XState actor rather than direct `router.push`; Pulse targets `/today`. Positive Leitsatz scheduling follows durable `guidingStatement` persistence, and editing/clearing/archiving/deleting it updates or cancels matching requests. `harmfulStatement` must never enter notification content or payloads. [Task 1]
- Expo Notifications supports repeating calendar/weekly triggers. Widgets and Live Activities require a development build; Expo SDK 57 `expo-widgets` is the first-party iOS path, Voltra is mainly for an explicit Android-widget requirement, and Live Activities are a poor default for daily reminders. [Task 1]
- Active schema version 2 stores `weekdays` and `times` on `ReminderAssignment`; guiding-belief assignments use `notificationContent` `general` or `leitsatz`, while Pulse assignments omit notification content. Migration `src/features/check-in/infrastructure/migrations/inline-reminder-timing.database-migration.ts` copies legacy schedule timing, maps `showFullText`, deletes legacy schedule rows, and fails closed with `Cannot migrate reminder assignment without its reminder schedule`. In-memory SurrealDB 3.1.2 coverage confirmed rollback without partial updates. [Task 2]
- `ConfirmedPickerModal` has a full-screen backdrop `Pressable` with `${testID}-backdrop` that calls `onDone`. Post-integration gates passed: `pnpm verify` 40 suites/270 tests, coverage (87.08% statements), and React Doctor 100/100; `.maestro/flows/reminder-owned-timing.yaml` parsed successfully. [Task 2]
- Expo map refresh reported 18 routes, 2 layouts, 30 screenshots, and 22 flows. `.expo-map/Youmotion-2026-08-20.appmap` is authoritative: `render-map.mjs` fails on format-v2 object flow steps with `TypeError: (f.steps ?? []).map is not a function`. Rebase, fast-forward, and push were verified at `afc5ce53874595dfd3055e77a7e5501f1f998c96`. [Task 2]
- The emotion check-in addition must reuse the local-first, assignment-owned subsystem: native requests remain derived projections, Pulse routes to `/today`, and notification taps route through the root navigation actor. Relevant paths are `src/features/reminders/`, `src/features/settings/ui/settings-screen.tsx`, `.maestro/flows/`, `docs/reminders-runtime-test-matrix.md`, and `docs/handoffs/`. [Task 4]
- The feature added localized Settings/reminder UI, focused tests, redacted Maestro lifecycle `.maestro/flows/emotion-check-in-reminder.yaml`, English/German screenshots, runtime/README/AGENTS updates, and `docs/handoffs/emotion-check-in-reminder.md` while preserving current reminder behavior. `pnpm verify` passed 40 suites/273 tests, Oxlint, and TypeScript 7. [Task 4]
- The current map artifact is `.expo-map/Youmotion-2026-08-21.appmap`: valid ZIP, unchanged graph (18 routes, 2 layouts, 0 edges), 22 flows, and 31 screenshots. Main and `origin/codex/emotion-check-in-reminder` were read back at `399fbbe4ec3767442620eeecaa8ba2784eac13f8` after a no-op rebase and `git merge --ff-only`. [Task 4]
- `src/features/reminders/ui/leitsatz-reminder-screen.tsx` reserves the `reminder-schedule-name-guidance-slot` at `minHeight: 38`; its regression test is `src/features/reminders/__tests__/leitsatz-reminder-screen.test.tsx`. Live iOS QA confirmed `TAGE` and `ZEIT` stay fixed while typing; `pnpm verify` passed 242 tests, coverage passed, and React Doctor scored 91/100 with one mapped-list warning in `reminder-settings-screen.tsx:55`. [Task 3]
- Commit only owned paths when unrelated artifacts exist. Commit `75496fdeb6fde1e081d9fa3978d142e312e970ee` was pushed to `codex/leitsatz-reminders`; EAS group `bad01098-0aad-46c1-9720-7384647e1835` was read back for Android/iOS at runtime `1.0.2` and the exact commit. Publish from a clean clone pinned to the pushed SHA with `CI=true pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --package-import-method=hardlink`; then use the existing `skills/youmotion-eas-update/SKILL.md` procedure. [Task 3]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: a hosted visual plan is required but cannot publish. Cause: the Plan connector is unavailable. Fix: do not improvise inline output; reconnect with `npx -y @agent-native/core@latest reconnect https://plan.agent-native.com --client codex`, restart, and publish through Plan. [Task 1]
- Symptom: persisted intent appears active while native reminders are wrong. Cause: requests were treated as stored truth. Fix: fingerprint/diff derived requests and run lifecycle/physical-device coverage for permission denial/revocation, foreground/background/terminated, reboot, update, timezone/DST, locale, test deep links, Android force-stop, stale targets, and Watch claims only after physical validation. [Task 1]
- Symptom: schedules are technically copied per reminder but UI/domain still exposes reusable names. Fix: remove the conceptual and persistence-level schedule abstraction, not only copy schedules. [Task 2]
- Symptom: Maestro reports `Unable to launch app com.youmotion.mobile: UNAVAILABLE: io exception` or Harness reports no Metro port in `8084-8093`. Cause: pre-flow environment failure. Fix: do not claim native validation; retry on a healthy dedicated target. The Expo map request was completed and included in the verified `.appmap` bundle. [Task 2]
import { useSelector } from '@xstate/react';
import { PressableScale } from 'pressto';
import { StyleSheet, Text, View } from 'react-native';
import { SafeAreaView } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';
import assert from '@/assert';

import {
  NAVIGATION_EVENTS,
  REMINDER_EVENTS,
  REMINDER_TARGET_KINDS,
} from '@/constants';
import { AppBackButton } from '@/components/ui/app-back-button';
import { PersistentScrollView } from '@/components/ui/persistent-scroll-view';
import { actionColors, palette, type } from '@/theme';
import { useAppLocale } from '@/localization/app-locale-provider';
import { formatWeekday } from '@/localization/date-copy';
import { useAppNavigationActor } from '@/navigation/app-navigation.provider';
import type { PulseReminderAssignment } from '../domain/reminder-assignment';
import {
  confirmReminderDeletion,
  deleteReminderAccessibilityLabel,
  deleteReminderText,
} from './reminder-deletion';

const _selectReminderContext = (
  snapshot: ReturnType<ReturnType<typeof useAppNavigationActor>['getSnapshot']>,
) => ({
  assignment: snapshot.context.reminderAssignments.find(
    (assignment) => assignment.targetKind === REMINDER_TARGET_KINDS.PULSE,
  ),
  error: snapshot.context.reminderError,
});

function PulseReminderCard({ assignment }: { assignment: PulseReminderAssignment }) {
  assert(assignment.weekdays.length > 0, 'Pulse reminder card requires weekdays');
  assert(assignment.times.length > 0, 'Pulse reminder card requires times');
  const actor = useAppNavigationActor();
  const locale = useAppLocale();
  const editReminder = () => actor.send({
    type: REMINDER_EVENTS.ASSIGNMENT_EDIT_REQUESTED,
    assignmentId: assignment.id,
  });
  const toggle = () => actor.send({
    type: REMINDER_EVENTS.ASSIGNMENT_TOGGLED,
    assignmentId: assignment.id,
  });
  const deleteAssignment = () => actor.send({
    type: REMINDER_EVENTS.ASSIGNMENT_DELETE_REQUESTED,
    assignmentId: assignment.id,
  });
  const confirmDelete = () => confirmReminderDeletion(deleteAssignment);
  const deleteAccessibilityLabel = deleteReminderAccessibilityLabel();

  return (
    <View style={styles.reminderCard} testID="reminder-assignment-card">
      <Text style={styles.assignmentSectionLabel}><fbt desc="Emotion check-in reminder assignment kind">EMOTION CHECK-IN</fbt></Text>
      <Text style={styles.assignmentTitle}><fbt desc="Emotion check-in reminder content description">Check in with your emotions</fbt></Text>
      <PressableScale accessibilityRole="button" onPress={editReminder} style={styles.reminderEdit} testID={`reminder-edit-${assignment.id}`}>
        <View style={styles.assignmentCopy}>
          <Text style={styles.reminderTiming}>
            {assignment.weekdays.map((weekday) => formatWeekday({ locale, weekday })).join(', ')} · {assignment.times.map(({ hour, minute }) => `${String(hour).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(minute).padStart(2, '0')}`).join(', ')}
          </Text>
        </View>
        <Text style={styles.editLabel}><fbt desc="Edit reminder button">Edit</fbt></Text>
      </PressableScale>
      <View style={styles.assignmentRow}>
        <Text style={styles.assignmentStatus}>
          {assignment.enabled
            ? <fbt desc="Enabled reminder assignment status">Active</fbt>
            : <fbt desc="Disabled reminder assignment status">Off</fbt>}
        </Text>
        <View style={styles.assignmentActions}>
          <PressableScale accessibilityRole="button" onPress={toggle} style={styles.toggleAction} testID={`reminder-assignment-toggle-${assignment.id}`}>
            <Text style={styles.toggleActionText}>
              {assignment.enabled
                ? <fbt desc="Turn reminder assignment off button">Turn off</fbt>
                : <fbt desc="Turn reminder assignment on button">Turn on</fbt>}
            </Text>
          </PressableScale>
          <PressableScale accessibilityLabel={deleteAccessibilityLabel} accessibilityRole="button" onPress={confirmDelete} style={styles.deleteAction} testID={`reminder-assignment-delete-${assignment.id}`}>
            <Text style={styles.deleteActionText}>{deleteReminderText()}</Text>
          </PressableScale>
        </View>
      </View>
    </View>
  );
}

export function ReminderSettingsScreen() {
  const actor = useAppNavigationActor();
  const { assignment, error } = useSelector(actor, _selectReminderContext);
  assert(assignment === undefined || assignment.targetKind === REMINDER_TARGET_KINDS.PULSE, 'Settings may only show the Pulse reminder');
  assert(assignment === undefined || assignment.id.length > 0, 'Displayed reminder must have an id');
  const _back = () => actor.send({ type: NAVIGATION_EVENTS.BACK_REQUESTED });
  const _newReminder = () => actor.send({ type: REMINDER_EVENTS.CREATE_REQUESTED });
  const _retry = () => actor.send({ type: REMINDER_EVENTS.RETRY_REQUESTED });

  return (
    <View style={styles.page} testID="reminder-settings-screen">
      <SafeAreaView edges={['top', 'bottom']} style={styles.safeArea}>
        <View style={styles.header}>
          <AppBackButton
            onPress={_back}
            testID="reminder-settings-back"
          />
        </View>
        <PersistentScrollView contentContainerStyle={styles.content}>
          <Text style={styles.eyebrow}><fbt desc="Emotion check-in reminder settings eyebrow">EMOTION CHECK-IN</fbt></Text>
          <Text style={styles.title}><fbt desc="Emotion check-in reminder settings title">A moment to notice how you feel.</fbt></Text>
          <Text style={styles.copy}><fbt desc="Emotion check-in reminder settings explanation">Choose when Youmotion may gently invite you to open the app and check in with your emotions. Leitsatz reminders live with each Leitsatz.</fbt></Text>
          {assignment ? <PulseReminderCard assignment={assignment} /> : null}
          {!assignment ? (
            <View style={styles.empty} testID="reminder-settings-empty">
              <Text style={styles.reminderTitle}><fbt desc="Empty emotion check-in reminder settings title">No emotion check-in reminder yet</fbt></Text>
              <Text style={styles.copy}><fbt desc="Empty emotion check-in reminder settings explanation">Add one when a gentle invitation to notice how you feel would help.</fbt></Text>
            </View>
          ) : null}
          {error ? (
            <View style={styles.errorCard}>
              <Text style={styles.error}>
                {error === 'Your reminders could not be loaded.'
